  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to use properties of the triangle and its circumcircle, along with the fact that the points \\(D, E, F\\) are the midpoints of the sides of \\(\\triangle ABC\\). This makes \\(\\triangle DEF\\) a medial triangle, and the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle DEF\\) is known as the nine-point circle of \\(\\triangle ABC\\). The nine-point circle has several interesting properties, including that it passes through the midpoints of the sides, the feet of the altitudes, and the midpoints of the segments from the vertices to the orthocenter.\n\nGiven that \\(D, E, F\\) are midpoints, the nine-point circle has a radius half that of the circumcircle of \\(\\triangle ABC\\). Also, the nine-point circle is the circumcircle of the triangle formed by the midpoints of \\(\\triangle ABC\\).\n\nWe need to find the sum \\(\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG}\\), where the arcs are measured in degrees. Since \\(D, E, F\\) are midpoints, the arcs \\(\\widehat{DE}\\), \\(\\widehat{HJ}\\), and \\(\\widehat{FG}\\) are related to the angles of \\(\\triangle ABC\\).\n\nFirst, we note that the angles of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) are \\(84^\\circ\\), \\(60^\\circ\\), and \\(36^\\circ\\). The arcs \\(\\widehat{DE}\\), \\(\\widehat{HJ}\\), and \\(\\widehat{FG}\\) are related to these angles. Specifically, \\(\\widehat{DE}\\) is the arc opposite the angle \\(36^\\circ\\), \\(\\widehat{HJ}\\) is the arc opposite the angle \\(60^\\circ\\), and \\(\\widehat{FG}\\) is the arc opposite the angle \\(84^\\circ\\).\n\nUsing the fact that the sum of the arcs on a circle is \\(360^\\circ\\), we can find the measures of these arcs:\n\\[\n\\widehat{DE} = 180^\\circ - 36^\\circ = 144^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\widehat{HJ} = 180^\\circ - 60^\\circ = 120^\\circ,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\widehat{FG} = 180^\\circ - 84^\\circ = 96^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nNow, we substitute these values into the expression \\(\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG}\\):\n\\[\n\\widehat{DE} + 2 \\cdot \\widehat{HJ} + 3 \\cdot \\widehat{FG} = 144^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 120^\\circ + 3 \\cdot 96^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nCalculating the right-hand side:\n\\[\n144^\\circ + 2 \\cdot 120^\\circ + 3 \\cdot 96^\\circ = 144^\\circ + 240^\\circ + 288^\\circ = 672^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{672}.\n\\]",
